## Make, Move, Delete

To be able to work within Linux, we need to know how we can make, move and delete folder and files. To start, lets make sure that we start in the `Intro_to_Linux` folder.

``` bash
cd ~/Intro_to_Linux/
```

First, we will take a look at creating directories. For this we can use the command `mkdir` (make directory). Lets start with creating two folders, temp1 and temp2

``` bash
mkdir temp1 temp2
```

As you can see, we create two folders in one go. The `mkdir` command can take multiple names and will create all the names separated by a space in the current directory, unless specifically told to make it somewhere else. Lets check if the directories have indeed been created.

``` bash
ls
```

\

