Because the file was copied, the current directory should still contain the file as well.

``` bash
ls 
```

Files can be moved using the `mv` (move) command. Similar to the copy command it takes the file which is to be move and location to which it should be moved.

``` bash
mv myfile2.txt ~/Intro_to_Linux/temp2/
```

